Design a 4-bit by 4-bit multiplier block that takes a 4-bit input and produces a 16-bit output. The module performs a series of bitwise operations, including shifts and additions, to compute the product. The output represents the result of multiplying the input value by 16, 256, and additional factors, effectively synthesizing the multiplication through combinational logic without using dedicated multiplication hardware.
