Design a simple instruction memory for a digital system that outputs specific 32-bit instruction values based on a provided 3-bit address input. The module maps addresses 0 through 7 to corresponding predefined instruction codes, returning a default instruction of zero if the address is outside this range. This effectively serves as a small, fixed instruction storage unit for a processor or controller in a digital design.
