Design a sign extender that converts a 4-bit signed integer input into a 16-bit signed integer output. The module checks the sign of the input; if negative, it outputs the absolute value extended with sign bits to maintain the sign in the 16-bit output. If the input is positive, it simply extends it with leading zero bits.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    output [15:0] out
);

