description:
Design a simple finite state machine (FSM) that detects a sequence of input bits. The FSM transitions through three states: an initial state (state0), an intermediate state (state1), and a final state (state2). The state transitions occur based on the value of the input, with specific transitions dependent on whether the input is a '0' or '1'. The output signal is high only when the FSM reaches the final state (state2), indicating that the desired sequence has been detected. The design effectively monitors the input to determine signal patterns over time, suitable for applications such as pattern recognition or sequence detection in digital communication systems.
module top_module(
  input in,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input in,
  output out
);parameter state0 = 2'b00; // initial state
parameter state1 = 2'b01; // intermediate state
parameter state2 = 2'b10; // final state

// define transitions between states
always @(in) begin
  case (state)
    state0: if (in == 1'b0) state <= state0; else state <= state1;
    state1: if (in == 1'b0) state <= state0; else state <= state2;
    state2: if (in == 1'b0) state <= state0; else state <= state2;
    default: state <= state0;
  endcase
end

// define output signal
assign out = (state == state2);

initial begin
  state <= state0;
end

// define current state
reg [1:0] state;

endmodule

