description:
Develop a circuit that performs an 8-bit binary multiplication. The module takes two 8-bit inputs, A and B, and produces a 16-bit output, Y, which represents the product of A and B. It employs a shift-and-add algorithm, where for each bit of A, if the bit is set, it adds the appropriately shifted version of B to an accumulating result. The final product is outputted as Y after computing the entire multiplication process.
module top_module(
    input [7:0] A,
    input [7:0] B,
    output reg [15:0] Y
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [7:0] A,
    input [7:0] B,
    output reg [15:0] Y
);reg [15:0] temp;

integer i;

always @(*) begin
    temp = 16'b0;
    for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin
        if (A[i]) begin
            temp = temp + (B << i);
        end
    end
    Y = temp;
end

endmodule

