description:
Design a clock divider circuit that generates a pulse output (cp) based on the input clock (clk). The output pulse will be high for one clock cycle when the counter reaches a value greater than 8000 and then reset the counter to zero. Meanwhile, the counter increments on each positive edge of the input clock, and while the count is below 8000, the output remains low. This module effectively creates a slower clock signal or a periodic signal from a faster input clock.
module top_module(
		input clk,
		output reg cp
		);

code:
module top_module(
		input clk,
		output reg cp
		);reg [20:0]cnt=0;

		always@(posedge clk)begin
			if(cnt > 8000)begin
				cp <= 1;
				cnt <= 0;
			end
			else begin
				cnt <= cnt + 1; 
				cp <= 0;
			end
		end
endmodule

