description:
Design a clock divider that takes an input clock signal (clk) and produces a divided output clock signal (clk_div). The module counts clock cycles using a 26-bit register (cnt) and, when the count reaches 62,500,000 (half of which is 31,250,000), it toggles the output clock signal, effectively generating a clock signal with a frequency that is divided by 2 relative to the input clock signal. The module also incorporates an asynchronous reset (rst) that resets the counter and output to their initial states.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input rst,
  output reg clk_div
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input rst,
  output reg clk_div
);reg [25:0] cnt;

  always@(posedge clk or posedge rst) begin
    if (rst) begin
      cnt <= 26'd0;
      clk_div <= 'b0;
    end
    else begin

      if (cnt == 62500000 - 1) cnt <= 26'd0;
      else cnt <= cnt + 1;

      if (cnt < 31250000 - 1) clk_div <= 'b0;
      else clk_div <= 'b1;
    end
  end

endmodule

